# 7. Pricing Models

Klaud offers three pricing models designed to support different partner needs, project stages, and levels of engagement. These models allow partners to access specialized VMware Cloud Foundation and private cloud expertise in a flexible, predictable, and commercially practical way.

All prices listed in this section are **partner net prices** in **USD**. They are intended for qualified partners only and are not designed as end-customer-facing prices. Partners may define their own resale pricing, margin, contractual terms, and customer-facing proposal structure.

Final pricing and scope are subject to technical validation, project complexity, delivery assumptions, and customer environment readiness.

---

## 7.1 Pricing Model Overview

Klaud’s pricing structure is organized into three commercial models:

| Model                                       | Description                                               | Best Used For                                                                                           |
| ------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Model 1 — On-Demand Hourly Services**     | Time-and-materials access to Klaud specialists            | Small tasks, pre-sales support, troubleshooting, advisory work, or initial engagements                  |
| **Model 2 — Fixed-Price Service Bundles**   | Scope-based pricing for defined services and deliverables | VCF deployments, upgrades, migrations, assessments, and technical add-ons                               |
| **Model 3 — Partner Expert Capacity Plans** | Prepaid expert hours with defined validity                | Partners with recurring project needs, multiple opportunities, or ongoing demand for specialist support |

These models may be used independently or combined depending on the opportunity. For example, a partner may begin with hourly pre-sales support, move into a fixed-price deployment bundle, and later use a Partner Expert Capacity Plan for ongoing design reviews, optimization, or escalation support.

