## 7.2 Model 1 — On-Demand Hourly Services

The On-Demand Hourly Services model provides flexible access to Klaud’s senior VMware and private cloud specialists on a time-and-materials basis.

This model is useful when the scope is small, exploratory, urgent, or not yet clearly defined. It is also a practical entry point for new partners that want to validate Klaud’s expertise before moving into a fixed-price or prepaid engagement model.

This is the most flexible model, but it is not the recommended model for full project delivery. For larger or well-defined projects, Klaud recommends using Fixed-Price Service Bundles or Partner Expert Capacity Plans.

### 7.2.1 Best Use Cases

On-Demand Hourly Services are best suited for:

* Technical advisory sessions
* Pre-sales support
* Opportunity qualification
* Customer-facing technical calls
* Design review
* Bill of materials review
* Troubleshooting
* Health check follow-up
* Upgrade planning support
* Small configuration tasks
* Project rescue assessment
* Second-opinion architecture review

### 7.2.2 Hourly Rates

| Service Type                               |                 Partner Net Rate |
| ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------: |
| Standard senior VMware consulting          |                    **$165/hour** |
| Principal architect / advanced specialist  |                    **$195/hour** |
| Emergency, after-hours, or weekend support |                    **$260/hour** |
| Onsite consulting day rate                 | **$1,850/day + travel expenses** |

### 7.2.3 Commercial Rules

| Item               | Rule                                                                  |
| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Minimum engagement | 10 hours                                                              |
| Billing increments | 4-hour blocks after the minimum engagement                            |
| Delivery model     | Remote by default                                                     |
| Onsite delivery    | Available by request and subject to scheduling                        |
| Travel expenses    | Billed separately                                                     |
| Availability       | Best effort, subject to resource availability                         |
| Payment terms      | Prepaid or approved partner terms                                     |
| After-hours work   | Must be approved in advance unless related to an emergency engagement |

### 7.2.4 Positioning Guidance

This model should be positioned as a flexible entry point, not as the most cost-effective way to deliver full projects.

Recommended partner message:

> On-demand hourly services are available for short-term support, advisory work, troubleshooting, and early-stage technical validation. For defined projects, Klaud recommends fixed-price service bundles to provide clearer scope, predictable pricing, and stronger delivery control.

